Your pushes are now end-to-end encrypted: only devices you sign in on can read them. Signing in shows a recovery key. Save it: it is the only way back to your pushes if you forget your password.

New in the menu: Delete account, and the app's version on the last line.

A link's icon now comes from Chrome or its page, never from Google. Notifications and search work on encrypted pushes, and an unconfirmed share is retried, not dropped. A push over the month's limit now says why it's removed.
